{% extends "papers/base.html.tera" %}
{% block title %}Text-model sources and attribution — Sinkland Papers{% endblock title %}
{% block research_content %}
<h1>Text-model sources and attribution</h1>
<p>Academic connective prose is generated from a transition model compiled from the reusable sources below. We extract and normalize prose, remove source metadata and non-prose elements, and transform it into word-transition counts. Source texts are not included in the runtime distribution. Generated titles, researchers, data, figures and references are original procedural constructions.</p>
<p>The real researchers listed here did not author our fictional papers and do not endorse this project. Sinkland is not affiliated with or endorsed by arXiv. The transition model and generated corpus-derived prose carry the applicable source attribution obligations; source licenses are linked below.</p>
{% for source in sources %}
<section class="source">
    <h2>{{ source.title | escape }}</h2>
    <p>{{ source.authors | join(sep=", ") | escape }}</p>
    <p><a href="{{ source.abstract_url | escape }}" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer">arXiv:{{ source.id | escape }}</a> · <a href="{{ source.license | escape }}" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer">{{ source.license | escape }}</a></p>
    <p>Transformation: {{ source.notes | escape }}</p>
</section>
{% endfor %}
{% endblock research_content %}
